# The closure stays with compiled code, and the program lays `mark` on it in sight: Link lists that name, and compiled code still takes `call` off Function.prototype without a look.
# The image lists the name beside the function, so the program's own store goes through, and so does another store under the same name. Any other name ends the process.
# `poke` is a free name that each run defines, and it is handed nothing: it takes the keeper out of the heap and reads the closure off it.
# What else is ruled out of a closure: what-is-ruled-out-of-a-closure-that-stays-with-compiled-code-ends-the-process.ir.
# OPTIONS: mechanisms=all
# RUN: run-in-shell globalThis.poke = () => { const run = aotFindObjectOfLayout(0).run; run.mark = "again"; print(run.mark); };
# CHECK: base 1 base 2 laid
# CHECK-NEXT: again
# CHECK-NEXT: base 1 base 2 {{*}}
# CHECK-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(OTHER): run-in-shell globalThis.poke = () => { aotFindObjectOfLayout(0).run.other = 1; print("went on"); };
# OTHER: bun: internal AOT error: object mutation check failed
# OTHER-NEXT: AddProperty on a closure of 'target'
# OTHER-NOT: went on
